=== meta ===
rule: TEST_DISABLED
title: a skipping conftest fixture beside an unrelated production edit is an unexplained collection control, not "no production change"
origin: issue #205, found building #199 row P5 - v0.5.0 blocked this diff, correctly, and printed NO_PROD_CHANGE_IN_DIFF over a diff that changes app/billing.py. The <suite> unit calls nothing, so the edit gives it no symbol-matched evidence; the escalator was chosen from that per-finding evidence instead of from the diff
=== before: tests/conftest.py ===
import pytest


@pytest.fixture
def db():
    return {}
=== after: tests/conftest.py ===
import pytest


@pytest.fixture
def db():
    return {}


@pytest.fixture
def needs_network():
    pytest.skip("network tests are disabled")
=== before: app/billing.py ===
def total():
    return 78.75
=== after: app/billing.py ===
def total():
    return round(78.75, 2)
=== head: tests/test_billing.py ===
from app.billing import total


def test_total(db):
    assert total() == 78.75
